<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second Treaty of Aliwal North</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1869</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Treaty of Aliwal North, Convention of Aliwal North · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/free-state-basotho-wars">Free State–Basotho Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Convention of Aliwal North was signed in February 1869 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and the Orange Free State after the wars between the Free State and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sotho-people">Basotho</a>. It fixed the boundary of Basutoland, which Britain had annexed in 1868, and confirmed the Free State's possession of the fertile lowlands west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caledon-river">Caledon River</a>, known to the Basotho as the Conquered Territory.</p></div>
